[TITLE:e200 Cores Certification - Required Reference Manuals and Information]

[INTRO]
This document lists the NXP/Freescale reference manuals and specific information
needed to complete the e200 cores certification improvements. Each manual section
is mapped to the certification requirements it supports.

[REF-MANUAL-001]
UID: REF-001
TITLE: e200z0 Core Reference Manual
DOCUMENT_NUMBER: E200Z0CRM
PUBLISHER: NXP Semiconductors (formerly Freescale)
STATUS: AVAILABLE
URL: https://www.elektronikjk.com/elementy_czynne/IC/E200Z0.pdf

REQUIRED_SECTIONS:
1. Instruction Timing and Latency Tables
   - All instruction latencies (integer, branch, load/store, multiply, divide)
   - Pipeline stage breakdown for each instruction type
   - Load-to-use latency specifications
   - Multiply instruction latency (currently modeled as 4 cycles)
   - Divide instruction latency (currently modeled as 34 cycles)
   - Branch misprediction penalty

2. Pipeline Architecture
   - Confirmation of 4-stage pipeline (IF, ID, EX, WB)
   - Functional unit descriptions (ALU, BU, LSU, MUL)
   - Resource sharing constraints
   - Bypass path specifications (GPR, CR bypasses)
   - Register forwarding latency

3. Interrupt Handling
   - IVOR (Interrupt Vector Offset Register) table
   - Interrupt context save requirements
   - Critical vs external interrupt differentiation
   - Special-purpose register save requirements for interrupts
   - Link register (LR) handling in interrupt context

4. Memory System
   - Cache architecture (if applicable)
   - Memory access timing
   - Memory barrier semantics (MSYNC, SYNC, ISYNC)

5. Exception Handling
   - Division by zero behavior
   - Integer overflow exception handling
   - Exception latency specifications

USED_FOR:
- CERT-001: Complete Pipeline Scheduling Model
- CERT-002: Fix Memory Stage Reference (COMPLETED)
- CERT-003: Interrupt Handler Context Save
- CERT-005: Exception Handling
- CERT-006: Memory Barrier Semantics
- CERT-010: Register Spill Timing

[REF-MANUAL-002]
UID: REF-002
TITLE: e200z4 Core Reference Manual
DOCUMENT_NUMBER: e200z4RM, Rev. 0, 10/2009
PUBLISHER: NXP Semiconductors (formerly Freescale)
STATUS: AVAILABLE
URL: https://www.elektronikjk.com/elementy_czynne/IC/E200Z4.pdf

REQUIRED_SECTIONS:
1. Dual-Issue Pipeline Architecture
   - Dual-issue pairing rules (exact combinations)
   - Dispatch port behavior (DIS0, DIS1)
   - Functional units: SU0, SU1, BU, LSU, MU, FPU/SPE
   - SU0 vs SU1 instruction restrictions
   - Resource conflict rules for dual-issue

2. Instruction Timing
   - Latency for paired vs unpaired instructions
   - SPE (Signal Processing Extension) instruction latencies
   - FPU instruction latencies
   - Load/store latency with bypass
   - Multiply instruction latency

3. Cache System
   - Instruction cache (ICache) specifications
   - Cache miss penalties
   - Cache coherency requirements

4. VLE (Variable Length Encoding)
   - 16-bit vs 32-bit instruction selection rules
   - Register constraints (R0-R7 for 16-bit forms)
   - Immediate value encoding constraints
   - Instruction alignment requirements

USED_FOR:
- CERT-001: Complete Pipeline Scheduling Model (dual-issue rules)
- CERT-004: VLE Register Constraints
- CERT-007: Deterministic Code Generation
- CERT-008: VLE Instruction Length Decoding
- CERT-009: VLE Immediate Boundary Conditions

[REF-MANUAL-003]
UID: REF-003
TITLE: e200z6 Core Reference Manual
PUBLISHER: NXP Semiconductors

REQUIRED_SECTIONS:
1. Single-Issue Pipeline Architecture
   - 7-stage pipeline details (IF1, IF2, ID, EX, MEM, WB1, WB2)
   - Unified 32KB L1 cache architecture
   - Resource sharing: MUL, FPU, LSU conflict rules
   - Functional unit pipeline stages

2. Instruction Timing
   - Load-to-use latency (currently modeled as 4 cycles)
   - FPU instruction latencies
   - Multiply instruction latency
   - Divide instruction latency (34 cycles mentioned in code)
   - Branch misprediction penalty (3 cycles in model)

3. Cache Coherency
   - Unified cache coherency protocols
   - Memory barrier requirements (MSYNC vs SYNC)
   - Store-before-load ordering guarantees
   - Cache line size and alignment

4. Exception Handling
   - Division exception behavior
   - FPU exception handling (FPSCR management)
   - Exception latency

USED_FOR:
- CERT-001: Complete Pipeline Scheduling Model
- CERT-005: Exception Handling
- CERT-006: Memory Barrier Semantics (unified cache)
- CERT-010: Register Spill Timing

[REF-MANUAL-004]
UID: REF-004
TITLE: e200z7 Core Reference Manual
DOCUMENT_NUMBER: E200Z7CRM
PUBLISHER: NXP Semiconductors

REQUIRED_SECTIONS:
1. Dual-Issue Pipeline Architecture
   - Dual-issue pairing rules (exact combinations)
   - ALU0 vs ALU1 restrictions
   - Pairing restrictions (instructions that can't pair)
   - SPE/FPU pairing rules
   - LSU pairing rules

2. Instruction Timing
   - Latency for paired instructions
   - SPE instruction latencies
   - FPU instruction latencies (including FPR bypass)
   - Divide instruction latency (32 cycles mentioned in code)
   - Multiply instruction latency (4 cycles)

3. Functional Units
   - ALU0 and ALU1 capabilities
   - MUL unit location (in ALU0)
   - SPE/FPU unit behavior
   - Bypass paths (GPR, CR, SPE, FPR)

USED_FOR:
- CERT-001: Complete Pipeline Scheduling Model (dual-issue)
- CERT-003: Interrupt Handler Context Save (SPE/FPU)
- CERT-007: Deterministic Code Generation

[REF-MANUAL-005]
UID: REF-005
TITLE: Power Architecture Book E Specification
PUBLISHER: Power.org or NXP/Freescale

REQUIRED_SECTIONS:
1. BookE Interrupt Model
   - IVOR (Interrupt Vector Offset Register) specifications
   - Critical interrupt (IVOR0) vs external interrupt (IVOR4)
   - Interrupt context save requirements
   - RFI and e_rfi instruction semantics

2. Memory Model
   - Memory ordering semantics
   - MSYNC vs SYNC vs LWSYNC semantics
   - Memory barrier ordering guarantees

3. Exception Model
   - Exception types and priorities
   - Exception handling requirements
   - Register state preservation

USED_FOR:
- CERT-003: Interrupt Handler Context Save
- CERT-006: Memory Barrier Semantics
- CERT-005: Exception Handling

[REF-MANUAL-006]
UID: REF-006
TITLE: VLE (Variable Length Encoding) Specification
PUBLISHER: NXP/Freescale or Power.org

REQUIRED_SECTIONS:
1. Instruction Encoding
   - 16-bit instruction encoding rules
   - 32-bit instruction encoding rules
   - Register encoding constraints (3-bit for R0-R7)
   - Immediate value encoding constraints

2. Instruction Alignment
   - 16-bit instruction alignment requirements (2-byte)
   - 32-bit instruction alignment requirements (4-byte)
   - Mixed-mode code boundaries
   - Instruction stream decoding rules

3. Immediate Value Constraints
   - s6imm: 6-bit signed immediate (-32 to 31)
   - u5imm: 5-bit unsigned immediate (0 to 31)
   - u7imm: 7-bit unsigned immediate (0 to 127)
   - u4imm: 4-bit unsigned immediate (0 to 15)
   - Boundary value handling

4. Register Constraints
   - 16-bit instructions require R0-R7
   - Register allocation implications
   - Instruction selection rules

USED_FOR:
- CERT-004: VLE Register Constraints
- CERT-008: VLE Instruction Length Decoding
- CERT-009: VLE Immediate Boundary Conditions

[INFO-REQUIREMENTS]

[INFO-TIMING]
UID: INFO-TIMING
TITLE: Critical Timing Information Needed

FOR_CERT_001:
1. Exact instruction latencies for all instruction classes
2. Pipeline stage breakdown with cycle counts
3. Bypass path latencies (how many cycles for forwarding)
4. Resource conflict resolution (when units are shared)
5. Branch misprediction penalties (exact cycles, not estimates)
6. Cache miss penalties (for WCET analysis)
7. Load-to-use latency with all bypass scenarios

FOR_CERT_005:
1. Division by zero exception behavior (hardware trap vs software check)
2. Exception handler latency
3. Integer overflow exception specifications
4. FPSCR exception flag behavior

FOR_CERT_006:
1. MSYNC instruction exact semantics
2. Unified cache coherency protocol details
3. Memory ordering guarantees
4. Cache line size and alignment requirements
5. Store buffer behavior

FOR_CERT_010:
1. Stack access latency
2. Cache behavior for stack accesses
3. Spill slot alignment requirements
4. Register save/restore instruction timing

[INFO-INTERRUPT]
UID: INFO-INTERRUPT
TITLE: Critical Interrupt Handling Information Needed

FOR_CERT_003:
1. IVOR table specifications (which interrupts map to which IVORs)
2. Critical interrupt (IVOR0) context save requirements
3. External interrupt (IVOR4) context save requirements
4. SPR registers that must be saved for each interrupt type
5. FPR registers that must be saved when FPU is used
6. FPSCR save/restore requirements
7. Link register (LR) handling in interrupt context
8. Nested interrupt handling rules
9. VLE mode interrupt return requirements (e_rfi usage)

[INFO-VLE]
UID: INFO-VLE
TITLE: Critical VLE Information Needed

FOR_CERT_004:
1. Exact register encoding for 16-bit instructions (3-bit = R0-R7)
2. Instruction selection rules (when 16-bit vs 32-bit form)
3. Register allocation requirements

FOR_CERT_008:
1. Instruction alignment rules
2. Instruction stream decoding algorithm
3. Error detection for misaligned/corrupted streams
4. Mixed-mode boundary handling

FOR_CERT_009:
1. Immediate value encoding algorithms
2. Boundary value handling (-32, 31, 0, 127, 15)
3. Truncation/extension rules
4. Error cases when immediate doesn't fit

[INFO-DUAL-ISSUE]
UID: INFO-DUAL-ISSUE
TITLE: Critical Dual-Issue Information Needed

FOR_CERT_001_AND_CERT_007:
1. Exact pairing rules for e200z4 and e200z7
2. Instructions that cannot pair
3. Resource conflict resolution when pairing
4. Latency differences between paired and unpaired execution
5. Deterministic pairing behavior requirements

[ACCESS_REQUIREMENTS]

LEGAL_ACCESS:
Most NXP/Freescale reference manuals require:
1. NDA (Non-Disclosure Agreement) with NXP/Freescale
2. Product licensing agreement
3. Account with NXP/Freescale support portal

PUBLIC_ACCESS:
Some information may be available in:
1. Public application notes
2. Errata documents
3. Community forums (limited)
4. Open-source projects using e200 cores

RECOMMENDED_APPROACH:
1. Contact NXP/Freescale support for e200 core documentation access
2. Request specifically:
   - e200z0/z4/z6/z7 Core Reference Manuals
   - BookE specification documents
   - VLE encoding specification
   - Application notes on interrupt handling
   - Timing analysis guidelines for WCET

[VALIDATION_REQUIREMENTS]

WHEN_MANUALS_OBTAINED:
1. Create validation test matrix mapping manual sections to code
2. Verify all instruction latencies match manual specifications
3. Verify all bypass paths are correctly modeled
4. Verify interrupt context save requirements match manual
5. Verify memory barrier semantics match manual
6. Verify VLE encoding constraints match specification
7. Create regression tests based on manual specifications
8. Document any discrepancies between current code and manuals
9. Update CompleteModel flags after validation

[PRIORITY]

HIGH_PRIORITY:
- e200z6 Core Reference Manual (most extensively used in codebase)
- e200z4 Core Reference Manual (dual-issue rules)
- BookE Interrupt Specification

MEDIUM_PRIORITY:
- e200z0 Core Reference Manual
- e200z7 Core Reference Manual
- VLE Encoding Specification

LOW_PRIORITY:
- Application notes and errata
- Timing analysis guidelines

